01:07:25.460 --> 01:07:29.380
- You mean I'm to die because you think if there's a crime

01:07:31.470 --> 01:07:36.940
then it must be punished, and it doesn't matter who is punished.

01:07:37.340 --> 01:07:37.840
Yes.

01:07:41.270 --> 01:07:48.400
You don't by any chance a Gilbert and Sullivan fan, are you?

01:07:48.990 --> 01:07:49.490
What?

01:07:52.890 --> 01:07:56.610
No, it's very funny, really.

01:08:00.060 --> 01:08:12.120
so I'm to die to preserve your sense of order yes you understand Lawrence you

01:08:12.120 --> 01:08:20.410
must die for me I understand but I won't die for you

01:08:20.410 --> 01:08:30.000
what does she wow so yeah by your cut the guy had a gun so that you are

01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:34.600
It would have been better to tell a lie if I brought it in.

01:08:34.600 --> 01:08:37.200
Hara Gunshon, Hara Gunshon!

01:08:38.230 --> 01:08:39.190
Stop it!

01:08:39.190 --> 01:08:53.360
Geitomu Jinshō, Ūkangyō, Tenōshō, Hokushō,

01:08:53.360 --> 01:08:59.860
Uzei Jinyōkai, Yōkō Fushigi, Itasennokubutsu,

01:09:00.250 --> 01:09:08.290
It's your gods.

01:09:10.970 --> 01:09:13.290
It's your bloody, awful, stinking gods.

01:09:15.300 --> 01:09:16.680
They made you what you are.

01:09:19.010 --> 01:09:21.890
Made a lot in whatever filthy hell they came from.

01:09:23.610 --> 01:09:24.070
Damn her!

01:09:24.860 --> 01:09:25.810
Damn you!

01:09:25.810 --> 01:09:27.810
Damn you!

01:09:31.920 --> 01:09:44.490
What will happen to Major Sellius?

01:09:45.030 --> 01:09:46.490
That is none of your business.

01:09:49.120 --> 01:09:52.170
You wouldn't execute Major Sellius.

01:09:53.200 --> 01:09:57.040
Crime like bringing a wireless into the ward.

01:09:57.860 --> 01:10:00.000
Your friend was a disappointment.

01:10:00.190 --> 01:10:05.320
meant to me. Do you want to see him before you die?

01:11:01.950 --> 01:11:03.250
Something's changed.

01:11:06.680 --> 01:11:07.900
I read it all wrong.

01:11:11.410 --> 01:11:12.470
I think you've had it.

01:11:16.460 --> 01:11:19.280
What?

01:11:19.490 --> 01:11:22.080
I think you've had it.

01:11:37.580 --> 01:11:38.880
He said something strange.

01:11:41.320 --> 01:11:44.590
He said, I'm disappointed in your friend.

01:11:49.750 --> 01:11:50.290
What is wrong?

01:12:04.060 --> 01:12:05.640
You'll do nothing individually.

01:12:07.440 --> 01:12:09.720
They went mad.

01:12:12.580 --> 01:12:19.560
I wish they'd stop it.

01:12:31.120 --> 01:12:35.440
I don't want to hate any individual Japanese.

01:12:35.440 --> 01:12:47.160
What's your Christian name, by the way?

01:12:47.160 --> 01:12:49.490
Charles.

01:13:05.150 --> 01:13:09.110
- Nothing!

01:13:09.110 --> 01:13:14.490
- What's up, John?

01:13:14.490 --> 01:13:23.870
- I was dreaming, dreaming about this woman.

01:13:23.870 --> 01:13:25.920
- Sounds like she cut it off.

01:13:33.480 --> 01:13:59.410
It only mattered twice, it only mattered twice.

01:14:00.990 --> 01:14:11.140
Before the fall of Singapore the streets were just packed with people everybody was trying to get out

01:14:15.570 --> 01:14:30.000
Hotels were packed screaming and shouting there was this woman was different from all the rest

01:14:30.000 --> 01:14:46.230
really didn't seem to be frightened i was frightened we talked about the war and she kept

01:14:46.230 --> 01:14:57.290
saying tell me the truth what's the truth i want to know the truth bloody silly question really

01:15:02.360 --> 01:15:07.610
Anyway, I finished to have breakfast together the next morning.

01:15:09.630 --> 01:15:11.470
And would you believe it, I was whipped off.

01:15:12.190 --> 01:15:12.410
Hmm?

01:15:12.870 --> 01:15:16.730
The attack had started.

01:15:17.690 --> 01:15:18.630
Japanese lad.

01:15:19.110 --> 01:15:25.400
Anyway, I got back to the hotel a few days later.

01:15:31.050 --> 01:15:32.270
She was still there.

01:15:33.540 --> 01:15:40.830
She was standing in exactly the same place that I'd left.

01:15:41.920 --> 01:15:45.860
It was as if she hadn't moved since I'd walked away.

01:15:47.610 --> 01:15:51.540
Like I'd run across the street from the back of a cigarette.

01:15:58.860 --> 01:16:00.000
I don't think I want to talk about this.

01:16:00.000 --> 01:16:01.250
anymore, eh?

01:16:36.400 --> 01:16:38.180
Is she eh?

01:16:38.180 --> 01:16:41.660
Who there?

01:16:41.660 --> 01:16:43.160
Yes.

01:16:43.160 --> 01:16:46.680
I suppose I...

01:16:46.680 --> 01:16:50.460
What's the matter?

01:16:50.460 --> 01:16:51.640
The past.

01:16:51.640 --> 01:16:54.320
Again and again.

01:16:54.320 --> 01:16:58.560
You've got me at it now, John.

01:16:58.560 --> 01:17:00.000
Who is she?

01:17:03.960 --> 01:17:08.970
I'm afraid I've not had many romantic interludes of great importance.

01:17:08.970 --> 01:17:11.780
My expertise lies in the field of betrayal.

01:18:03.710 --> 01:18:06.790
- Where do you find the time to compose these songs?

01:18:06.790 --> 01:18:08.870
- While you're at school.

01:19:17.920 --> 01:19:21.510
- Why?

01:19:21.510 --> 01:19:22.510
- I laugh too.

01:19:22.510 --> 01:19:23.630
- They're after me.

01:19:23.630 --> 01:19:28.390
They hate me, they like you.

01:19:28.390 --> 01:19:30.000
- Don't worry, I won't let them touch you.

01:19:30.120 --> 01:19:36.850
straight ahead and go on home. Don't look back no matter what. Understand? Do what I told you.

01:20:00.540 --> 01:20:12.480
brave hey hunchback get out of the way

01:21:11.960 --> 01:21:14.120
You brought the pasta. Why'd you have to interfere?

01:21:14.120 --> 01:21:16.840
I told you what to do. Why don't you go home like I said?

01:21:16.840 --> 01:21:18.880
I'm sorry.

01:21:18.880 --> 01:21:20.100
No, you're not.

01:21:44.970 --> 01:21:50.080
- Stop crying.

01:21:50.080 --> 01:21:51.190
- You hate me too.

01:22:34.480 --> 01:22:37.840
brother was scared out of his skin when the time came for him to go to school I

01:22:37.840 --> 01:22:44.230
was in the sixth form top of my class and head of my house even so my brother

01:22:44.230 --> 01:22:58.060
lived every day in absolute terror being revealed tomorrow's the initiation any

01:22:58.060 --> 01:23:00.000
exemptions one chap's got a

01:23:00.030 --> 01:23:06.230
weak heart but he's got a doctor's certificate the one who's blind as a bat he can't even pee

01:23:06.230 --> 01:23:14.000
straight you've got a younger brother in your house haven't you yes i have what about him well

01:23:14.000 --> 01:23:20.810
what about him i was merely wondering if you he's all right he's perfectly all right forgive me

01:23:20.810 --> 01:23:27.120
but if there's any reason why i'd want your brother excused it's awfully decent of you but

01:23:27.120 --> 01:23:30.000
there's no reason honestly

01:23:45.550 --> 01:23:48.730
was waiting for me. But I couldn't conscience the thought of the whole

01:23:48.730 --> 01:23:53.850
school setting eyes on his back. It would reflect on me. I couldn't bear the

01:23:53.850 --> 01:23:56.670
thought that anything related to me was not of the best.

01:23:56.670 --> 01:24:00.000
I asked the master to let me stay after class to

01:24:00.510 --> 01:24:02.690
for the experiments the next day.

01:24:50.090 --> 01:24:52.310
What can you do?

01:25:30.410 --> 01:25:31.030
I'll see you next time.

01:27:16.120 --> 01:27:19.650
- So how did it go today?

01:27:19.650 --> 01:27:22.590
- You mean you didn't see?

01:27:22.590 --> 01:27:25.400
- No, I was in the science laboratory all afternoon.

01:27:25.400 --> 01:27:28.230
Had to finish a job for the science master.

01:27:28.230 --> 01:27:29.440
I've only just finished, in fact.

01:27:31.280 --> 01:27:39.300
My brother never sang another note, ever.

01:27:42.120 --> 01:27:44.200
He took over our father's farm in due course.

01:27:45.800 --> 01:27:47.340
Last time I saw him was at his wedding.

01:27:49.770 --> 01:27:57.330
Over the years, I became, you might say, a haunted person.

01:28:00.000 --> 01:28:11.300
really wanted to see him again. I never did. I was 32, eligible bachelor, reasonably successful

01:28:11.300 --> 01:28:26.460
lawyer, and absolutely nothing. When war broke out, I embraced it. Some inexplicable sense

01:28:26.460 --> 01:28:30.000
of relief kind of enthusiasm I hadn't.

01:28:30.830 --> 01:28:33.420
Shown for anything for how long?

01:28:34.680 --> 01:28:36.980
Join the Foreign Legion, Jack.

01:28:37.960 --> 01:28:39.420
It's been an easier life.

01:28:40.470 --> 01:28:42.260
It's the last thing I want.

01:28:45.340 --> 01:28:47.250
Ah, here comes the milkman now.

01:28:48.170 --> 01:28:48.970
Two pints.

01:28:50.190 --> 01:28:51.630
Shouldn't we order an extra one?

01:28:51.670 --> 01:28:52.630
It's Christmas, remember?

01:28:52.890 --> 01:28:54.070
Heavens, Christmas already.

01:28:54.190 --> 01:28:56.110
Well, it was lovely chatting, but I really must fly.

01:28:56.610 --> 01:28:57.470
It's not you.

01:28:57.870 --> 01:28:58.750
Come for me.

01:28:58.750 --> 01:28:59.570
Come for me.

01:29:07.290 --> 01:29:08.930
John, you're always wrong.

01:29:47.080 --> 01:29:51.920
Sir Sergeant Hara, you're human after all.

01:29:51.920 --> 01:29:56.160
Nani?

01:29:56.160 --> 01:30:00.000
Haragunson, anata mo yap parini.

01:30:03.450 --> 01:30:09.160
Florence-san, Puzzle Christmas, do you know?

01:30:09.160 --> 01:30:14.700
She's anxious.

01:30:14.700 --> 01:30:26.660
She's anxious, Farrah-san. Puzzle Christmas, Santa Claus, right?

01:30:26.660 --> 01:30:30.000
Come here!

01:30:30.220 --> 01:30:54.450
he thinks he's santa claus father father christmas

01:31:08.730 --> 01:31:12.680
We're free.

01:31:33.800 --> 01:31:36.880
Thank you.

01:32:11.290 --> 01:32:30.000
Representative Kuryo is here.

01:32:30.350 --> 01:32:40.690
- Everyone's here. - Lawrence, why are you here?

01:32:41.560 --> 01:32:44.120
I released him last night.

01:32:44.280 --> 01:32:45.010
What?

01:32:45.800 --> 01:32:47.860
I researched it again.

01:32:48.630 --> 01:32:51.060
The radio was found in the detention center.

01:32:52.180 --> 01:32:57.000
The 7th Brigade's officer, Chorakuen, took it.

01:32:57.160 --> 01:33:00.000
He confessed, so I recorded it.

01:33:00.540 --> 01:33:01.600
I executed him right away.

01:33:03.040 --> 01:33:06.820
It was my fault for making Lawrence the culprit.

01:33:07.020 --> 01:33:08.120
Why didn't you report it?

01:33:08.590 --> 01:33:11.800
When I got there, Jack Serriaz was executed as well.

01:33:12.510 --> 01:33:13.860
You didn't know?

01:33:15.800 --> 01:33:19.100
I was a little drunk.

01:33:20.200 --> 01:33:25.890
But I don't think that Lawrence or Serriaz would be of any help to us.

01:33:27.150 --> 01:33:29.640
They wouldn't be of any help to us.

01:33:30.000 --> 01:33:40.520
I believe that the man is able to fix it.

01:33:40.520 --> 01:33:42.910
Captain Yonoi,

01:33:42.910 --> 01:33:46.650
whatever happened to your idea to replace me with Major Sellers?

01:33:46.650 --> 01:33:53.870
Shut up, sir.

01:33:53.870 --> 01:33:56.730
First here in the camp.

01:33:56.730 --> 01:33:57.870
There are none here, sir.

01:33:57.870 --> 01:34:00.000
Not one among 600 men.

01:34:00.760 --> 01:34:03.680
Do you think you can get away with such an obvious lie?

01:34:03.680 --> 01:34:09.030
I'm told it is the Japanese way to lie, sir.

01:34:09.030 --> 01:34:10.650
Very well.

01:34:10.650 --> 01:34:14.750
All prisoners on parade in five minutes.

01:34:14.750 --> 01:34:23.130
Dismissed!

01:34:23.130 --> 01:34:24.900
I said everyone!

01:34:40.300 --> 01:34:47.640
I'm responsible for the construction of the Halku Air Base.

01:35:03.840 --> 01:35:08.960
Let's get it done and ban it.

01:36:04.280 --> 01:36:07.190
- What are they up to now?

01:36:07.190 --> 01:36:11.050
- I don't think it's anything fairly routine stuff this.

01:36:11.050 --> 01:36:11.650
Don't worry.

01:36:36.590 --> 01:36:37.710
- Listen, John.

01:36:37.710 --> 01:36:41.870
- What?

01:36:41.870 --> 01:36:42.710
- I wish I could sing.

01:37:27.040 --> 01:37:27.750
It is beautiful.

01:37:34.060 --> 01:37:36.430
- My orders were explicit.

01:37:36.430 --> 01:37:40.990
I said that all prisoners were to assemble.

01:37:40.990 --> 01:37:43.760
You are not all here.

01:37:43.760 --> 01:37:47.210
- We are all here, sir.

01:37:47.210 --> 01:37:58.330
- You, come here.

01:37:58.330 --> 01:37:59.760
You lied to me again.

01:38:00.830 --> 01:38:05.580
I said all prisoners, where are the men from the hostels?

01:38:05.580 --> 01:38:07.880
They can't possibly be moved.

01:38:07.880 --> 01:38:11.150
All prisoners will assemble immediately.

01:38:11.150 --> 01:38:13.220
Get them! Now, get them!

01:39:50.730 --> 01:39:53.550
Captain, that's against the Geneva Convention, those are sick men.

01:39:53.550 --> 01:39:56.200
Red, stop it, stop it.

01:39:56.200 --> 01:39:57.240
Stop it, don't you, mate?

01:39:57.240 --> 01:40:00.000
Stop it, don't you, don't you?

01:40:00.920 --> 01:40:21.760
I'm going to die.

01:40:57.640 --> 01:40:58.610
I'm going to tell you, Lloyd!

01:41:03.870 --> 01:41:04.520
Stand!

01:41:33.130 --> 01:41:35.700
Come here! Now! Come here!

01:41:35.700 --> 01:41:53.690
As a representative of the British Air Force,

01:41:53.690 --> 01:41:58.930
how many experts in weapons and guns do you have in your group?

01:42:00.000 --> 01:42:06.500
sir.

01:43:13.880 --> 01:43:15.110
Let's go.

01:44:28.670 --> 01:44:29.480
It's night.

01:44:30.000 --> 01:44:34.980
of Sentimental, as Captain Annoyed.

01:44:34.980 --> 01:44:38.360
Things will be different now.

01:45:31.980 --> 01:45:32.580
It's out.

01:45:36.360 --> 01:45:39.070
It's out.

01:45:40.500 --> 01:45:40.800
Teacher!

01:45:41.770 --> 01:45:42.350
Teacher!

01:45:44.690 --> 01:45:45.830
Teacher will advise!

01:45:46.520 --> 01:45:47.320
Fly the lift!

01:46:25.950 --> 01:46:30.000
I don't understand them, do you?

01:46:31.630 --> 01:46:32.950
Commit horror carry!

01:49:37.680 --> 01:49:39.050
I'm pleased to see you.

01:49:39.050 --> 01:49:40.070
Really, Jack?

01:49:40.070 --> 01:49:41.730
I wanted to come.

01:49:41.730 --> 01:49:44.980
Don't apologize.

01:49:44.980 --> 01:49:50.480
Wrong, Jill.

01:49:50.480 --> 01:49:53.880
Help me water these things.

01:50:02.040 --> 01:50:05.490
- I need to talk with you.

01:50:05.490 --> 01:50:10.490
- Hey, remember this one?

01:50:10.490 --> 01:50:13.280
Flowers once, every five years.

01:50:13.280 --> 01:50:18.120
That's all.

01:50:18.120 --> 01:50:19.270
- Flowers again.

01:50:36.750 --> 01:50:37.990
through the moon.

01:54:43.850 --> 01:54:48.430
And you? You would come, Mr. Lawrence?

01:54:48.430 --> 01:54:51.250
You've learned English?

01:54:51.250 --> 01:54:55.510
Yes. Very little. Please.

01:55:02.680 --> 01:55:10.380
- I very nearly didn't get you a message.

01:55:10.380 --> 01:55:11.140
- Tomorrow morning.

01:55:30.280 --> 01:55:35.730
It was up to me. I'd release you today, send you back to your family.

01:55:35.730 --> 01:55:42.460
Thank you.

01:55:42.460 --> 01:55:44.880
I am ready to die.

01:55:44.880 --> 01:55:55.250
I don't understand. My crimes were no different from any other soldiers.

01:56:14.680 --> 01:56:17.000
You're the victim of men who think that they're right.

01:56:20.060 --> 01:56:28.130
Just as one day you and Captain Yonoi believed absolutely that you were right.

01:56:33.680 --> 01:56:37.960
Truth is, of course, nobody's right.

01:56:41.490 --> 01:56:50.350
Do you remember Jack Selliers?

01:56:51.720 --> 01:56:53.200
Strange.

01:56:54.390 --> 01:56:56.370
I dreamed of him last night.

01:56:57.770 --> 01:56:59.360
Really?

01:57:09.370 --> 01:57:13.570
Captain Yunori gave me a lock of Jack Sellier's hair

01:57:13.570 --> 01:57:17.640
and asked me to take it to his village in Japan

01:57:17.640 --> 01:57:21.940
and dedicate it to his shrine.

01:57:21.940 --> 01:57:29.700
He said he was executed

01:57:39.150 --> 01:57:51.300
It was as if Selliers, by his death, sowed a seed in Yonoi, that we might all share by its growth.

01:57:57.890 --> 01:57:59.230
Do you remember?

01:58:00.000 --> 01:58:26.020
that Christmas good Christmas wasn't it it was a wonderful Christmas you were drunk may I go on

01:58:26.020 --> 01:58:28.320
and on being drank

01:58:31.050 --> 01:58:32.070
Saki is wonderful.

01:58:33.690 --> 01:58:34.090
Thank you.

01:58:35.250 --> 01:58:36.170
Father Christmas.

01:58:36.700 --> 01:58:37.250
Thank you.

01:59:12.350 --> 01:59:22.890
of times when victory is very hard to take.

01:59:22.890 --> 01:59:28.450
- You might have a son.

01:59:28.450 --> 01:59:29.700
- God bless you.

01:59:38.670 --> 01:59:46.070
Merry Christmas, Merry Christmas, Mr. Lawrence.
